uilibrio electrolítico.\",86\r\n7833,HIPONATREMIA,DC,Hiponatremia is a condition that has been reported in patients undergoing dietary treatment,85\r\n7864,HIPONATREMIA,HORMONAS TIROIDEAS,Hormonas tiroideas can affect sodium levels and contribute to the development of hiponatremia,84\r\n7827,HIPONATREMIA,DIABETES INSÍPIDA,Diabetes insipidus can lead to hyponatremia due to excessive fluid loss and electrolyte imbalance,83\r\n7850,HIPONATREMIA,HIPERGLUCEMIA,\"Hyponatremia can be secondary to hyperglycemia, complicating its diagnosis\",82\r\n7835,HIPONATREMIA,DIETA HIPOSÓDICA,La dieta hiposódica puede causar hiponatremia en pacientes con alteraciones renales o en tratamiento con diuréticos,81\r\n7844,HIPONATREMIA,NP,\"Hyponatremia was studied in NP patients, showing a correlation with their hospital stay\",80\r\n7875,HIPONATREMIA,TOLVAPTÁN,\"Tolvaptán is used to treat hyponatremia, particularly in patients with heart failure\",77\r\n4384,ASCITIS,HIPONATREMIA,La ascitis puede ser un signo de hiponatremia hipervolémica en los pacientes,77\r\n7859,HIPONATREMIA,DIURÉTICOS,\"Hyponatremia is a condition characterized by low sodium levels in the blood, and diuretics are medications commonly used to manage fluid retention associated with this condition. However, it is important to note that diuretics can also lead to hyponatremia, as they promote the loss of sodium and water from the body. Thus, while diuretics can be beneficial in managing fluid retention in patients with hyponatremia, they also carry the risk of exacerbating the condition by causing further sodium depletion.\",73\r\n7846,HIPONATREMIA,ESTANCIA HOSPITALARIA,Hyponatremia can lead to longer hospital stays for patients,73\r\n7857,HIPONATREMIA,INSUFICIENCIA CARDIACA,\"Hiponatremia is a condition characterized by low sodium levels in the blood, which can be caused by insuficiencia cardiaca (heart failure). In patients with insuficiencia cardiaca, fluid retention and altered sodium levels contribute to the development of hiponatremia. This condition often arises as a complication in these patients, primarily due to fluid imbalance resulting from the heart's inability to pump effectively. Thus, there is a clear relationship between hiponatremia and insuficiencia cardiaca, where the latter can lead to the former through mechanisms of fluid retention and sodium dysregulation.\",73\r\n7845,HIPONATREMIA,TRATAMIENTO,Effective treatment of hyponatremia can reduce mortality rates,72\r\n7825,HIPONATREMIA,NATREMIA,\"Hyponatremia and natremia are closely related concepts in the context of sodium levels in the blood. Hyponatremia is defined by abnormal natremia levels, specifically when sodium concentrations are low. Natremia serves as a critical measurement for diagnosing and managing hyponatremia, as it directly indicates the presence of low sodium levels in the bloodstream. Therefore, natremia levels are essential for both the diagnosis and management of hyponatremia, highlighting the importance of monitoring sodium concentration in the blood for effective medical intervention.\",71\r\n7867,HIPONATREMIA,ACIDOSIS METABÓLICA,\"Acidosis metabólica can occur alongside hyponatremia, indicating a complex interplay of electrolyte imbalances\",71\r\n7862,HIPONATREMIA,HIPOALDOSTERONISMO,\"Hipoaldosteronismo is a condition characterized by insufficient levels of aldosterone, a hormone that plays a crucial role in regulating sodium retention in the body. This deficiency can lead to hiponatremia, which is a condition marked by low sodium levels in the blood. The impaired sodium retention caused by hipoaldosteronismo results in the development of hiponatremia, highlighting the interconnectedness of these two conditions.\",70\r\n7874,HIPONATREMIA,DESMOPRESINA,Desmopressin is administered in the treatment of hyponatremia to regulate sodium levels,70\r\n12979,SIADH,DIURÉTICOS,The use of diuretics can complicate the diagnosis of SIADH due to their effect on sodium levels,69\r\n7869,HIPONATREMIA,EDEMA C